Description: Edition only: hand a failed AppStream cache compile to sparky-stereo-problems
 Daniel, 2026-11-01: "nothing we do should silently fail or have a fall back - either it works or not and the user must know".
 When appstreamcli cannot compile a catalog's cache, flatpak-appstream-cache.patch warns in the log and Discover loads the
 catalog in its own process, about 1 GB of memory, and the person never learns why.
 The edition's one engine for failures (sparky-stereo-problems, ORDER 350) keeps the problem in the person's store, with the
 catalog, the reason and what to do, in the nine languages (the package's lang/ files built into journal catalogs), shows it
 through its session notifier, and clears it at the next successful compile.
 One key per catalog (appstream-cache- and a hash of the arguments). Not for Debian or KDE: this file only adds the call.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
